/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 6.5 University Review & Examination Questions) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Q1: Explain the purpose and operation of Context Managers \('with' statement\) in) Tj
T*
(Python file I/O.) Tj
T*
(Answer: The 'with' statement simplifies resource management by guaranteeing that setup) Tj
T*
(and teardown actions occur reliably around a block of code. For file I/O, 'with) Tj
T*
(open\(...\) as f:' binds the opened stream to f. Internally, the context manager calls the) Tj
T*
(__enter__\(\) method when entering the block, and guarantees that __exit__\(\) is executed) Tj
T*
(upon leaving the block \(even if a critical exception occurs, an unhandled error is) Tj
T*
(raised, or a return statement is executed\). This prevents file descriptor leaks,) Tj
T*
(operating system resource exhaustion, and file corruption caused by unclosed buffers.) Tj
T*
(* Q2: Describe the role of 'else' and 'finally' blocks in Python exception handling.) Tj
T*
(Answer: In a try-except structure: The 'except' block catches and handles designated) Tj
T*
(exceptions that occurred during try execution. The 'else' block executes ONLY if the try) Tj
T*
(block completes successfully with ZERO exceptions raised. It isolates code that should) Tj
T*
(not be accidentally monitored by the try handlers. The 'finally' block executes) Tj
T*
(unconditionally in all circumstances: whether an exception was raised, caught,) Tj
T*
(re-raised, or if no exception occurred. It is reserved for essential resource cleanup,) Tj
T*
(such as closing network sockets, database connections, or freeing hardware locks.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 6.6 Key Takeaways and Revision Points) Tj
T*
